dax: a read of the page its entry names replaces nothing

A filesystem says a read's pages are shared, as XFS does of reflinked
blocks and Fxfs of blocks in a region other files map, so that
dax_associate_entry counts their folios' sharers. dax_insert_entry took
that for a change of page: it unmapped the page from everything mapping
it, and replaced the entry with its like. Two processes reading a page
then undid each other's mappings, one fault for each load, each taking
the entry's lock and a TLB shootdown: a build's processes running one
binary out of a filesystem's shared blocks stopped, their tasks queued
on the entries of its hot pages (fxdax TASK-152). A read of the page its
entry names, or its PMD entry's row, leaves the entry and the page's
other mappings alone, as an unshared read does. Writes still replace it:
a CoW fault's dirty and TOWRITE marks go with the replacing.

diff --git a/fs/dax.c b/fs/dax.c
--- a/fs/dax.c
+++ b/fs/dax.c
@@ -1035,6 +1035,18 @@ static bool dax_fault_is_synchronous(const struct iomap_iter *iter,
 		(iter->iomap.flags & IOMAP_F_DIRTY);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Whether real entry @entry names @pfn as the page of @index already, a PMD
+ * entry the page of its row.
+ */
+static bool dax_entry_names(void *entry, unsigned long index, unsigned long pfn)
+{
+	if (dax_is_zero_entry(entry) || dax_is_empty_entry(entry))
+		return false;
+	index = dax_is_pmd_entry(entry) ? index & PG_PMD_COLOUR : 0;
+	return dax_to_pfn(entry) + index == pfn;
+}
+
 /*
  * By this point grab_mapping_entry() has ensured that we have a locked entry
  * of the appropriate size so we don't have to worry about downgrading PMDs to
@@ -1050,7 +1062,14 @@ static void *dax_insert_entry(struct xa_state *xas, struct vm_fault *vmf,
 	void *new_entry = dax_make_entry(pfn, flags);
 	bool write = iter->flags & IOMAP_WRITE;
 	bool dirty = write && !dax_fault_is_synchronous(iter, vmf->vma);
-	bool shared = iter->iomap.flags & IOMAP_F_SHARED;
+	/*
+	 * A read of a shared page its entry names replaces nothing. Replacing it
+	 * anyway unmaps the page from everything else mapping it, which faults
+	 * again and unmaps it from this mapping in turn: tasks reading one page
+	 * take a fault for each load, queued on its entry.
+	 */
+	bool shared = (iter->iomap.flags & IOMAP_F_SHARED) &&
+		      (write || !dax_entry_names(entry, xas->xa_index, pfn));
 	/*
 	 * A shared fault replacing a PMD entry with a PTE entry splits it: else
 	 * its store over the PMD's multi-index slot names the one page for all
